%% Reader question: What identity, context, work, policy, capability, artifact, and evidence cross each boundary in the reference implementation?
%% Evidence cutoff: 2026-07-11
%% Claim status: C4 container reference design using illustrative component categories; exact private topology, configuration, and enforcement are not publicly reproducible
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Container view and boundary-crossing data
    accDescr: An operator sends intent and human decisions to a local agent client. A mediated access component receives caller identity and a bounded context request. Persistent domain agents and temporary execution workers are separate runtime principals. A queue receives work identity and lease state. Version control and delivery receive source revisions and artifacts. Memory returns authorized source identity, cutoff, and bounded content. An authorization policy produces an allow, deny, or human-gate decision; a separate credential issuer returns a short-lived capability reference only after approval. External calls carry the authorized operation and capability. Telemetry receives revision, artifact, work, and observed-outcome identity and creates evidence-backed repair work. These are distinct functional and authorization boundaries, not one shared trust zone.

    O["Person: Operator"]

    subgraph SYS["System: Operating agent system"]
    subgraph LOCAL["Boundary: Operator-controlled client"]
      C["Container: Local agent client"]
    end

    subgraph ACCESS["Boundary: Mediated access"]
      A["Container: Context and dispatch mediator"]
    end

    subgraph DOMAIN["Boundary: Persistent role principal"]
      D["Container: Domain-agent service"]
    end

    subgraph WORKER["Boundary: Temporary worker principal"]
      W["Container: Execution worker"]
    end

    subgraph QUEUE["Boundary: Durable work state"]
      Q["Container: Lease-based work queue"]
    end

    subgraph VERSIONED["Boundary: Versioned source and delivery"]
      G["Container: Repositories, review, CI, and declarative rollout"]
    end

    subgraph MEMORY["Boundary: Scoped knowledge"]
      M["Container: Authoritative records and rebuildable recall"]
    end

    subgraph POLICY["Boundary: Authorization policy"]
      P["Container: Consequence and scope evaluator"]
    end

    subgraph CREDENTIAL["Boundary: Credential custody"]
      I["Container: Scoped capability issuer"]
    end

    subgraph EVIDENCE["Boundary: Evidence and telemetry"]
      T["Container: Tests, traces, checks, and live probes"]
    end
    end

    E["External system: System of record or action target"]

